lines+=['', '## 2. Generalized family description', '', 'Given a two-dimensional conservative field and an oriented curve, recover a potential from both gradient components, find ordered endpoints from the path, and subtract f(end)−f(start). Moderate sources give the parametrization and conservative hint; hard sources establish conservativeness on R² and parametrize a supplied Cartesian curve. Each potential/path family is a same-level variation, not a progression. Integer powers, familiar sine/cosine evaluations, exact logarithms/exponentials and perfect-square radical evaluations remain as observed.', '', '## 3. Component and complete-bank map', '', 'All observed profiles are named observed_homogeneous within their own template. The only replay parameter freedom is F↦sF, f↦sf, and each option↦s times its complete source-shaped expression, s=1,2,3; path and relative coefficients remain fixed. This is a coherent field-scale operation, not an arbitrary fitted error polynomial. Exact expressions are observed evidence; the original author’s incorrect operation is unresolved except where obvious. These replay banks are not default banks and do not establish the authored variety claim.', '', '| Source | Field UUID | Source answer UUID | Correct? | Exact observed value | Replay expression |', '|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
