lines+=['', '## 4. Reusable templates and workload bounds', '', 'Fixed parts: source prose, theorem, reconstruction instructions, constant-C explanation, endpoint wording, one worked solution independent of selected option, field layout and option count. Variable parts are complete field components, complete potential, complete path components/interval, cross derivative (hard only), endpoint coordinate tuples and arithmetic rows. Inline endpoint prose uses a whole-sentence mask; no arbitrary short-expression substitution occurs. Standard TeX replaces the source Unicode invisible function-application and underbrace glyphs; this normalization is reported separately from prose/sequence fidelity.', '', 'Final arithmetic uses separate per-family masks: ordered uncomputed substitution; then simplified endpoint values for one-term potentials, uncollected term evaluations for cubic/exponential and separated-cubic potentials, grouped zero contributions for the hard sine/exponential potentials, retained trig factors for sin(x)sin(y), and distributed then collected arithmetic for the radical-path source. Original row counts and operation stages are retained at changed parameters. Final collection/factorization occurs only in the last row.', '', '| Template | Level | Explicit sampling bounds | Substantive endpoint arithmetic |', '|---|---|---|---|']
for template,(level,sid) in g.TEMPLATES.items():
 terms={'easy_product':1,'easy_separable':2,'quartic_trig':1,'cubic_exponential':3,'exponential_cosine':1,'cubic_product':2,'separable_cubic':3,'cosine_product':2,'radial_log':1,'sine_exponential':2,'mixed_exponential':2,'sine_product':1,'negative_exponential':2,'cubic_radical_path':2}[template]
 lines.append('| '+template+' | '+level+' | `'+json.dumps(g.BOUNDS[template],sort_keys=True)+'` | '+str(2*terms)+' full potential-term substitutions across two endpoints |')
lines+=['', 'All a,b,c coefficients are nonzero; signed absolute magnitudes are at most 3. Easy uses integer endpoints, one product term or two uncoupled quadratic terms. Moderate keeps the observed powers/potential families and at most three terms, with original familiar trig/log/exp endpoints. Hard keeps at most two potential terms (or the radial logarithm), equal continuous mixed partials on R², and the original path complexity. The radical-path n=1,2 makes both endpoint radicands perfect squares; logarithmic path arguments are positive over the full interval.', '', 'The easy scope is authored because no practice source has an easy label. It is anchored to canonical e-8760, the actual lesson route and the Calculating Potential Functions prerequisite: reconstruct a simple potential before subtracting values at a supplied linear path’s endpoints. Both easy templates require the KP-defining reconstruction. There is no conservative-existence check or new branch at easy.', '', 'Default complete authored bank: I; −I (reverse endpoints); 2I (double every coefficient while reconstructing f); I/2 (halve every coefficient while reconstructing f); 0 (subtract the same endpoint value twice). These are explicit full operations on the reconstructed potential/endpoints. Reject the entire instance if any member is equivalent; with this bank that means I=0. No first-valid recipe pool, source-choice sampling or learner-facing error diagnosis is used.', '', 'Source profiles fix relative parameters; authored defaults independently vary coefficients/path parameters. The canonical mathematical fingerprint uses the displayed field and ordered endpoints, omitting banks/profiles and curve parameters that cannot affect endpoints; the full presentation identity includes version, level, exact prompt, fixed solution, entire bank and domain. Easy zero-result paths and any other zero-result instance are rejected with their entire bank; explicit invalid inputs raise rather than resample.', '', '### Source errors and repairs', '', '- q-104747: r(0)=⟨0,2⟩ is correct, but the next prose sentence says (0,0). The path y=exp(sin x)+cos x gives y(0)=2. Generated prose uses (0,2). The final f(0,2) and bank are already correct.', '- q-104764: endpoints/substitution correctly use (0,−e), but the symbolic final f subtraction says f(0,e). The path y=x²−exp(sqrt(x+1)) gives y(0)=−e. Generated subtraction uses f(0,−e). Numerically both evaluate to zero because x=0; this does not make the incorrect coordinate acceptable.', '', 'No options or correct designations are erroneous. Exact unrepaired endpoint solution denominator is 10/12, repaired solution denominator is 2/12; complete bank/value/designation fidelity remains 12/12. Original raw errors remain in source.json, source-cases.json and original review sections.']
